open-switcher (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=high

  * Close H-08 by delegating input ACLs to seat-aware logind uaccess and
    revoking an already-open backend whenever the authorized session changes.
  * Close M-09 by bounding package shutdown, rejecting replacement of a live
    daemon, and narrowly cleaning verified legacy input ACL entries.
  * Require current-tag semantics from udev 247 and avoid stale sticky tags or
    manifest-free retriggers while removing package-owned input access.
  * Close L-02 by keeping one canonical package-owned udev rule and applying it
    before systemd's seat-late uaccess processing.

 -- Andrey Mukha <6871314+andreymukha@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 03:00:31 +0300

open-switcher (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=high

  * Preserve and acknowledge deferred physical input only after the virtual
    keyboard writer has completed the corresponding mutation.
  * On Cinnamon/X11, hold the text tail after a deferred focus-switch chord
    until the active target changes or the bounded fail-open deadline expires.

 -- Andrey Mukha <6871314+andreymukha@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:44:29 +0300

open-switcher (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Require acknowledged virtual keyboard writer shutdown before backend
    recovery, and fail-stop the daemon for a clean systemd restart on timeout.
  * Close the physical keyboard fd immediately if EVIOCGRAB release fails.

